{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And Israel was saved.</b> Now Israel was saved from the hand of Egypt, for until now the fear of the king was upon them. And it is written that the Egyptians sank in the sea, and the sea did not cast them onto the dry land, for thus it is written תִּבְלָעֵמוֹ אָרֶץ (below, 15:12). Therefore it explains, \"And Israel saw Egypt dead on the shore of the sea\" — that Israel was on the shore of the sea and saw Egypt dead as they sank:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:33.755281141Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}